Power Saver (like Zorin OS)
--------------------------

tammoOS includes a Zorin OS-style Power Saver. It lives in the `powersaver/` folder.

What it gives you:
- Power profiles: Power Saver, Balanced and Performance, the same backend (power-profiles-daemon) that Zorin OS uses
- On tammoOS 2.x the profiles also show up in Settings -> Power and in the Quick Settings menu, and the system switches to Power Saver automatically when the battery runs low
- On tammoOS 1.x (Ubuntu 18.04 base) it uses TLP as the power backend, since that base has no power-profiles-daemon
- Battery percentage in the top bar, screen dimming and automatic suspend

Install it (after a normal tammoOS install):

    sudo bash powersaver/install.sh

Then use it from a terminal:

    tammo-powersaver status     show the active power profile
    tammo-powersaver set power-saver|balanced|performance
    tammo-powersaver toggle     flip between balanced and power-saver

There is also a "tammoOS Power Saver" entry in the applications menu.
